    {
      "title": "Asiad 2026: India bag silver in 10m air rifle team event; 3rd medal overall",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/sports/asian-games/asiad-2026-india-bag-silver-in-10m-air-rifle-team-event-3rd-medal-overall-126092100062_1.html",
      "description": "India clinched a silver medal in the men's 10m air rifle team event at the Asian Games here on Monday, with shooters Rudrankksh Patil and Himanshu Dhillon also qualifying for the individual final.\nRudrankksh, Himanshu and Parth Mane finished with a team total of 1890.1.\nChina claimed the gold with a world record team total of 1899.0 points, bettering their previous mark by 0.6 points.\nSouth Korea produced a strong fightback but had settle for bronze with a total of 1884.2 points.\nRudrankksh finished with a score of 631.8 points to occupy third place in the individual qualification standings, while Himanshu's 630.0 put himself in seventh.\nParth, on the other hand, missed out on a place in the individual final after finishing 10th with 628.3 points.\nThe silver added to India's medal tally in shooting, which had begun with another second-place finish in the women's 10m air rifle team.\nElavenil Valarivan, Sonam Maskar and Vidarsa Vinod combined to win silver for India in the women's",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-21T02:52:29"
    }
